  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_039_WindowsAccount
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-039
  title: Wrong kind of permission
  category: 3
  content: 'There are two independent permission systems in play and they are easy
    to confuse. The POS staff role (KB-008) governs what a person may do inside the
    till. The Windows account governs whether the application may run at all.

    A
    POS that will not start while the staff account reads perfectly correct is the
    Windows layer. Check who the machine is signed in as before touching anything
    in Staff Management.'
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P39
